  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Isaiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 22,
    "summary": "Jerusalem will be attacked and scourged—The people will be carried captive—The Messiah will hold the key of the house of David, inherit glory, and be fastened as a nail in a sure place.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The burden of the valley of vision. What aileth thee now, that thou art wholly gone up to the housetops?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "IE a message of doom to Jerusalem."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 22:1",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou that art full of stirs, a tumultuous city, a joyous city: thy slain men are not slain with the sword, nor dead in battle.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "OR noise."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 80
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 22:2",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "All thy rulers are fled together, they are bound by the archers: all that are found in thee are bound together, which have fled from far.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 117
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 22:3",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore said I, Look away from me; I will weep bitterly, labour not to comfort me, because of the spoiling of the daughter of my people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Mourning."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
